Wait for the "File not in cwd. Change cwd to ...?" prompt before opening the tree.

M.execute falls through to do_show_or_focus right after starting
inputs.confirm, so the tree is opened while the popup is the current window and
is closed together with it: the split fails ("Invalid window id" in nui,
then E95 "Buffer with this name already exists" on every later open) and the
file's window is left showing a neo-tree buffer with no state.tree (E5108 on any
key). The confirm callback already calls do_show_or_focus once the question is
answered, so the call must not also run unconditionally.

Regression from #2063 (3f7289e), present in 3.42.0 and on main.
Upstream: https://github.com/nvim-neo-tree/neo-tree.nvim/issues/2121
Drop this patch once a release contains the fix.

--- a/lua/neo-tree/command/init.lua
+++ b/lua/neo-tree/command/init.lua
@@ -229,6 +229,7 @@
           do_show_or_focus(args, state, force_navigate)
         end
       )
+      return
     end
   end
   args.dir = args.dir or cwd
